# Copy to .env and fill in

# --- Firebase (v2.1a) --------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="growline-dev"

# Browser-side, for phone auth only. These are public by design — they identify
# the project, they do not authorise anything. Access is controlled by Security
# Rules, never by hiding these.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""

# --- App Check ---------------------------------------------------------------
# What this protects is the BILL, not the data — Security Rules already handle the
# data. The project id is public by design and Phone auth is enabled, so without
# App Check anyone can drive OTP sends at the project, and SMS to Indian numbers is
# billed per message.
#
# BLANK IS SAFE AND IS THE DEFAULT. With no site key the client does nothing at
# all, which is what keeps CI and every local emulator run byte-identical. It is
# also skipped automatically whenever an emulator host is set above, because a real
# reCAPTCHA key cannot attest 127.0.0.1.
#
# ⚠ ORDER: ship the app with this key set BEFORE turning enforcement on in the
# Firebase console. Enforcement with no attesting client rejects every Auth and
# Firestore request — that is an outage, not a hardening. See HANDOFF.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_SITE_KEY=""
# "enterprise" (default, and what the cutover runbook registers) or "v3". This must
# match what the console was actually set up with; a mismatch fails attestation with
# an error that names neither side.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_PROVIDER="enterprise"
# A debug token from the browser console, for running against a REAL project from a
# developer machine. Never set in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN=""

# Set to point the browser at the Auth emulator. Test numbers configured there
# return a fixed code, so the login flow runs with no SMS and no reCAPTCHA.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:9099"

# Browser-side Firestore emulator host. Needed by the realtime QR listener, which
# runs in the page and so cannot see the server-only variable below. Without it the
# browser talks to a REAL project while the server talks to the emulator, and every
# live update silently never arrives — nothing errors, the row just never appears.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined at build time, so change this and rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:8080"

# Set BOTH to work against the local emulators (npm run emulators), or NEITHER to
# point at a live project. With both set, no credentials are needed and the
# migration script refuses to touch a real project.
#
# The app refuses to boot on one without the other, and names the one that is
# missing. Emulator routing is resolved PER PRODUCT by the Admin SDK, so a single
# flag cannot describe the state: with only the Auth host set, real data is read
# and written while ID-token and session-cookie signatures are never checked at
# all — the emulator verifier accepts `alg: none`. That is one line in a deploy
# config away from accepting an unsigned cookie naming any uid.
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:8080"
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:9099"

# Production only: the service-account JSON, on one line. Never commit a real one.
# The app refuses to start if neither this nor an emulator host is set, so a
# missing credential fails at boot rather than at the first query.
#
# It also refuses to start if this is set at the same time as the two emulator
# hosts above: the hosts win, so the credential would be decoration on a process
# that looks like production. Comment the hosts out before filling this in. An
# empty value is treated as unset, so this file works as-is.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=""

# Admin panel (F12). Comma-separated user ids allowed to open /admin.
#
# An env allowlist rather than a database flag ON PURPOSE: it means becoming an admin
# requires a deploy, reviewed by whoever deploys, and it cannot be granted by anything
# that can write to Firestore. There will be one to three admins, so the friction is free.
#
# Blank — the default — means /admin returns 404 in this deployment. An unset variable
# never means "everyone is an admin".
#
# The panel shows COUNTS ONLY. Prospect names and phone numbers are never visible there;
# see src/lib/admin.ts for why that is the line.
ADMIN_UIDS=""

# Demo mode. Set to "1" to enable /demo — sign in as a seeded coach with no SMS, and
# switch between a senior coach, a mid-line coach and a new coach in one tap. For showing
# the app to somebody on the spot, where an OTP round trip kills the moment.
#
# It is NOT an auth bypass: it mints a real session for a real seeded user, so every
# screen afterwards runs the production code path under the real Security Rules. The uid
# comes from a fixed table in src/lib/demo.ts and never from the request.
#
# NEVER SET THIS ON THE REAL PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT. With it unset, /demo and
# /api/demo/session both answer 404 and no demo UI renders anywhere. There is no second
# way in — no query parameter, no header, no "unless localhost" check.
#
# Requires the seed: `npm run db:seed` then `npm run migrate:firestore`.
DEMO_MODE=""

# --- Legacy (SQLite; removed once v2.1a cutover completes) -------------------
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
# 32+ random bytes, hex — signs session JWTs
SESSION_SECRET=""
# Public origin, no trailing slash, e.g. https://growline.in
# Used for QR capture URLs, snapshot links and Open Graph images. Falls back to the
# request host when unset, which is fine for local dev but wrong behind a proxy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=""

# Web push (follow-up reminders). Generate a pair with:
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys --json
# The public key is sent to the browser; the private key signs pushes and must not
# be exposed. Notifications simply stay off if these are unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=""
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=""
VAPID_SUBJECT="mailto:support@growline.in"

# Shared secret for the daily reminder job at /api/notifications/daily.
# The endpoint refuses to run without it, so an attacker cannot trigger a send.
CRON_SECRET=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Razorpay Subscriptions — the Leader tier (v2 §8, Phase 9b, D75).
#
# Payments stay OFF until all five are set: `isConfigured()` is the single switch every
# money route checks, and with any of these blank the subscribe button says "not switched
# on" and does nothing. Nothing is ever charged by accident.
#
# Two are SECRETS and must never be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or logged:
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET      pairs with the key id; signs the checkout callback
#   RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET  set when you register the webhook URL in the dashboard;
#                            every event is HMAC-verified against it before parsing
#
# The two plan ids are created ONCE in the Razorpay dashboard (Subscriptions → Plans):
#   ₹999  monthly  →  RAZORPAY_PLAN_MONTHLY
#   ₹9,999 yearly  →  RAZORPAY_PLAN_ANNUAL
#
# Webhook URL to register:  https://<your-domain>/api/payments/webhook
# Events to subscribe:      subscription.* (all of them)
#
# Growline never sees or stores a UPI id, card, or bank detail (RULES L7). The mandate is
# authenticated inside Razorpay's own checkout; this app receives ids and signatures only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
RAZORPAY_PLAN_MONTHLY=""
RAZORPAY_PLAN_ANNUAL=""

# --- Privacy notice (v2 §5.4) ------------------------------------------------
# Four facts no code can derive. Until ALL FOUR are set, /privacy returns 404 and
# nothing links to it — a notice with "TBD" where the grievance officer should be
# is worse than no notice, because it looks like a legal commitment while failing
# the one duty it exists to discharge.
#
# DPDP Rules 2025 require a NAMED human as grievance officer; "support team" does
# not satisfy it. The postal address is required too — an email alone does not.
PRIVACY_ENTITY_NAME=""
PRIVACY_GRIEVANCE_OFFICER=""
PRIVACY_GRIEVANCE_EMAIL=""
PRIVACY_POSTAL_ADDRESS=""
